#: apps/reports/structure.py:26
msgid ""
"We used the boundary you gave us; we did not survey it. Only a sworn "
"surveyor (géomètre) can confirm the boundary and area on the ground, and "
"only the land registry can confirm who owns the land."
msgstr ""
"We used the boundary you gave us; we did not survey it. Only a sworn "
"surveyor (géomètre) can confirm the boundary and area on the ground, and "
"only the land registry can confirm who owns the land."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:31
msgid ""
"Population figures are estimates from computer models, not census counts. "
"They are less reliable for small areas, and future figures are projections. "
"Ages and sexes come from one profile per region, so they describe the "
"region, not the neighbourhood. Local statistics or a visit may give a "
"different picture."
msgstr ""
"Population figures are estimates from computer models, not census counts. "
"They are less reliable for small areas, and future figures are projections. "
"Ages and sexes come from one profile per region, so they describe the "
"region, not the neighbourhood. Local statistics or a visit may give a "
"different picture."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:37
msgid ""
"Travel times are calculated on roads mapped by volunteers (OpenStreetMap), "
"without traffic. Unmapped tracks, closed roads or rainy-season conditions "
"can change them. Visit the site to see how it is really reached."
msgstr ""
"Travel times are calculated on roads mapped by volunteers (OpenStreetMap), "
"without traffic. Unmapped tracks, closed roads or rainy-season conditions "
"can change them. Visit the site to see how it is really reached."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:42
msgid ""
"The flood data only covers large rivers, at about 90 m detail: it does not "
"show flooding from heavy rain, blocked drains or the sea. Slopes come from "
"30 m elevation data that includes buildings and trees. Neighbours' "
"experience and a visit in the rainy season remain essential."
msgstr ""
"The flood data only covers large rivers, at about 90 m detail: it does not "
"show flooding from heavy rain, blocked drains or the sea. Slopes come from "
"30 m elevation data that includes buildings and trees. Neighbours' "
"experience and a visit in the rainy season remain essential."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:48
msgid ""
"We can only check rules that appear on the maps we have. Many constraints, "
"such as planned roads, local zoning or customary claims, are not mapped. The"
" commune's urban planning office and the land registry have the final word."
msgstr ""
"We can only check rules that appear on the maps we have. Many constraints, "
"such as planned roads, local zoning or customary claims, are not mapped. The"
" commune's urban planning office and the land registry have the final word."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:53
msgid ""
"Satellite images have 10 m pixels: they show what generally covers the land,"
" not small buildings. The building map can be a few years old and miss "
"recent or small structures. Only a visit tells you who is on the land today."
msgstr ""
"Satellite images have 10 m pixels: they show what generally covers the land,"
" not small buildings. The building map can be a few years old and miss "
"recent or small structures. Only a visit tells you who is on the land today."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:58
msgid ""
"Changes are measured on 10 m satellite pixels with one image a year; clouds,"
" seasons and small parcels make the figures indicative only. Very recent "
"work may not show yet."
msgstr ""
"Changes are measured on 10 m satellite pixels with one image a year; clouds,"
" seasons and small parcels make the figures indicative only. Very recent "
"work may not show yet."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:64
msgid ""
"We only find what the news outlets we follow published online, checked by an"
" analyst. Many disputes are never reported: ask neighbours and the local "
"authorities."
msgstr ""
"We only find what the news outlets we follow published online, checked by an"
" analyst. Many disputes are never reported: ask neighbours and the local "
"authorities."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:72
msgid ""
"This report is a first look at a location, built from free public data: "
"satellite images, open maps and global models. It is not a land title "
"search, a survey or a valuation."
msgstr ""
"This report is a first look at a location, built from free public data: "
"satellite images, open maps and global models. It is not a land title "
"search, a survey or a valuation."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:77
msgid ""
"Each finding says what the data suggests. Data can be coarse, incomplete or "
"out of date: more detailed data or a visit to the site may show something "
"different."
msgstr ""
"Each finding says what the data suggests. Data can be coarse, incomplete or "
"out of date: more detailed data or a visit to the site may show something "
"different."

#: apps/reports/structure.py:81
msgid ""
"Use it to decide what to check, and always confirm on the ground, with a "
"sworn surveyor (géomètre), the land registry and the commune, before paying "
"anything."
msgstr ""
"Use it to decide what to check, and always confirm on the ground, with a "
"sworn surveyor (géomètre), the land registry and the commune, before paying "
"anything."

